        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Milada Šubrtová, Leoš Janáček, Antonín Dvořák\n- Organizations: National Theatre in Prague\n- Works: Jenůfa, Rusalka\n- Concepts: Rusalka, Slavic mythology\n\nFacts:\n- Milada Šubrtová was born on 24 May 1924 and died on 1 August 2011.\n- Milada Šubrtová was a Czech operatic soprano.\n- Milada Šubrtová had a lengthy career at the National Theatre in Prague from 1948 through 1991.\n- Milada Šubrtová received particular acclaim for portraying the title heroines in Leoš Janáček's Jenůfa and Antonín Dvořák's Rusalka.\n- A rusalka is a water sprite from Slavic mythology that usually inhabits a lake or river.",
